Z||000003||Raydar||12-30-2001||10:27 PM||||Hmmm... Not sure about an 84. <BR>I just disassembled an 88 Formula with cruise. <BR>What I'm sure you'll need are:<BR>The module.<BR>The wiring harness between the module and the main cabin harness. <BR>A clutch and/or brake switch.<BR>The turn signal stalk with the wire. <BR>The vacuum canister/servo unit.<BR>The throttle cable from the servo to the TBI.<P>The engine compartment cruise control wiring is actually part of the tail-light harness on the 88. Probably previous years, too.<P>Not sure if there is anything else or not.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||12-30-2001||11:06 PM||||You'll need all of the wiring associated with the cruise system.  84's that didn't come with cruise from the factory have none of the wires in the harness.  As a point of trivia, the 84's with factory cruise had the cruise electronics built into the speedometer circuit board.  They didn't use a separtate module until 85.  Even the speedometer circuit board is different on a cruise equipped 84 and a non-cruise equipped 84!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
